('1b5f378d-00a6-5299-b320-a71cdae150cc','662b8bcd-2336-5a62-a9bb-d16d653a2338',5,null,null,'law','the period of time when someone is below the age at which they become legally responsible for their actions','[ uncountable ]',null,'دوره زمانی که شخصی کمتر از سنی است که از نظر قانونی مسئول اعمال خود می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a small minority She is one of a small minority of women working in engineering.','a tiny minority Only a tiny minority of the population actually commit crimes.','a large minority A large minority of women feel happier when their husbands leave them.','a substantial/sizeable minority (= a large minority ) A sizeable minority of people sleep less than five hours a night without problems.','a significant minority (= a large and fairly important minority ) A significant minority of older people have difficulty in caring for themselves.','be in a minority Male students are in a minority in this class.','represent a minority Old people still only represent a minority of the population.','form a minority ( also constitute a minority formal ) This type of cell forms a minority of the cells in the nervous system.','affect a minority The side effects only affect a minority of people who take the drug.','a minority group It’s ridiculous to refer to women as a minority group.','a minority interest Jazz is a minority interest, but it is still an important part of musical studies.','a minority opinion/view This is a minority view among scientists.','a minority stake (= a number of shares in a company, equalling less than half the total number ) IBM has bought a minority stake in the computer company.','a minority shareholder (= someone who owns less than half the shares in a company ) A minority shareholder with 10% of voting rights refused to accept the plan.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('fb5f82e7-3eba-5955-8c8f-c20ff0a0ab08','1f5ad9cc-e261-5290-83ed-46604ab00ec1',1,null,null,'spoken & written','in addition – used to introduce information that adds to or supports what has previously been said',null,null,'افزون بر این، علاوه بر آن؛ همچنین','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The rent is reasonable and, moreover, the location is perfect.","translation":"اجاره مناسب است و علاوه بر این، موقعیت مکانی عالی است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000209819.mp3"},{"sentence":"The source of the information is irrelevant. Moreover, the information need not be confidential.","translation":"منبع اطلاعات بی ربط است. علاوه بر این، اطلاعات لازم نیست محرمانه باشد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001755073.mp3"},{"sentence":"The rent is reasonable and, what’s more , the location is perfect.","translation":"اجاره مناسب است و علاوه بر این، موقعیت مکانی عالی است.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,3),
('7574f5dc-d0a7-5f1e-83aa-058e3b9e9b3a','0a6c6d21-a8a7-5788-9d46-1031579e2df2',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a legal arrangement by which you borrow money from a bank or similar organization in order to buy a house, and pay back the money over a period of years',null,null,'رهن، رهن (خانه)؛ رهن (پول)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have a mortgage They have a mortgage on a small house in North London.','take out a mortgage (= borrow money to buy a house ) We took out a 25-year mortgage.','get a mortgage We couldn''t get a mortgage.','pay/repay a mortgage If I lose my job, we won''t be able to pay the mortgage.','pay off a mortgage (= finish paying all the money you owe ) They paid off their mortgage five years early.','fall/get behind with the mortgage (= be unable to pay enough money each month ) He fell behind with the mortgage when he lost his job.','big/high They both need to work full-time because their mortgage is so big.','cheap (= with a low interest rate ) Homebuyers are eager to take advantage of the cheap mortgages on offer.','a mortgage payment If interest rates go down, your mortgage payments will fall.','the mortgage rate (= the rate of interest you will pay on a mortgage ) You need to shop around for a good mortgage rate.','a mortgage lender (= a bank that provides mortgages ) Nearly all mortgage lenders plan to raise their interest rates.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Your building society or bank will help arrange a mortgage.","translation":"انجمن ساختمانی یا بانک شما به ترتیب وام مسکن کمک می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000210485.mp3"},{"sentence":"They’ve taken out a 30-year mortgage (= they will pay for their house over a period of 30 years ) .","translation":"آنها یک وام مسکن 30 ساله گرفته اند (= هزینه خانه خود را در مدت 30 سال پرداخت خواهند کرد).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001554897.mp3"},{"sentence":"We decided to use Fred’s redundancy money to pay off the mortgage (= pay back all the money we borrowed for a mortgage ) .","translation":"ما تصمیم گرفتیم از پول اضافی فرد برای پرداخت وام مسکن استفاده کنیم (= تمام پولی را که برای وام مسکن قرض گرفته‌ایم پس بدهیم).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001554904.mp3"},{"sentence":"Mortgage rates are set to rise again in the spring.","translation":"قرار است نرخ وام مسکن در بهار دوباره افزایش یابد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001554911.mp3"},{"sentence":"She was having trouble meeting her mortgage payments .","translation":"او در پرداخت وام مسکن خود مشکل داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001554915.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('2bfedf3b-460b-565c-922c-d3911a62273c','0a6c6d21-a8a7-5788-9d46-1031579e2df2',2,null,null,'spoken & written','the amount of money you borrow in the form of a mortgage',null,null,'مقدار پولی که در قالب وام مسکن قرض می گیرید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have a mortgage They have a mortgage on a small house in North London.','take out a mortgage (= borrow money to buy a house ) We took out a 25-year mortgage.','get a mortgage We couldn''t get a mortgage.','pay/repay a mortgage If I lose my job, we won''t be able to pay the mortgage.','pay off a mortgage (= finish paying all the money you owe ) They paid off their mortgage five years early.','fall/get behind with the mortgage (= be unable to pay enough money each month ) He fell behind with the mortgage when he lost his job.','big/high They both need to work full-time because their mortgage is so big.','cheap (= with a low interest rate ) Homebuyers are eager to take advantage of the cheap mortgages on offer.','a mortgage payment If interest rates go down, your mortgage payments will fall.','the mortgage rate (= the rate of interest you will pay on a mortgage ) You need to shop around for a good mortgage rate.','a mortgage lender (= a bank that provides mortgages ) Nearly all mortgage lenders plan to raise their interest rates.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"If you earn £20,000 per year, then you may be able to get a mortgage of £60,000.","translation":"اگر سالانه 20000 پوند درآمد دارید، ممکن است بتوانید 60000 پوند وام مسکن دریافت کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000210499.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('31aca904-aa36-50ae-a27c-8c07aee75627','54b60b00-9013-5cab-83c4-1dc788d5171d',1,null,null,'spoken & written','if you mortgage your home , land , or property , you borrow money, usually from a bank, and if you cannot pay back the money within a particular period of time, the bank has the right to sell your property in order to get the money you owe it',null,null,'اگر خانه، زمین یا ملک خود را رهن می کنید، معمولاً از بانک وام می گیرید، و اگر نتوانید پول را در مدت زمان معینی پس دهید، بانک حق دارد ملک شما را بفروشد تا پولی را که به آن مدیون هستید به دست آورد.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"We mortgaged our house to start Paul’s business.","translation":"ما خانه خود را رهن کردیم تا تجارت پل را راه اندازی کنیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000210509.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('289cfa62-6ac7-5f3c-81d6-0ca993002e58','54b60b00-9013-5cab-83c4-1dc788d5171d',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'mortgage the/somebody’s future',null,'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('1d1e4c81-6bb9-5dbc-a669-4a93de6520c0','8259cc04-d330-533d-87d9-5c2d561d2965',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a very wide road for travelling fast over long distances , especially between cities',null,null,'اتوبان، بزرگراه (بریتانیایی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['drive on/along/down the motorway He was driving along the motorway at a steady sixty miles an hour.','get on/off the motorway We got on the motorway near Watford.','join the motorway (= get on the motorway ) Traffic will be diverted through Hamilton before joining the motorway.','leave the motorway A few miles further on they left the motorway.','turn off the motorway (= leave the motorway ) We forgot to turn off the motorway and ended up in London.','busy The motorway is always busy around Birmingham.','a major motorway Two of Britain''s major motorways pass through Nottingham.','a six-lane/eight-lane etc motorway There are plans to build a new six-lane motorway through the area.','motorway driving Is motorway driving included in the driving test?','motorway traffic the constant noise of motorway traffic','a motorway crash Six people were killed in a motorway crash.','a motorway pileup (= when several cars on a motorway crash into each other ) a news report of a motorway pileup on the M25','a motorway junction (= a place where you can join or leave the motorway ) Their stores are all situated near major motorway junctions.','a stretch/section of motorway This stretch of motorway is always very busy.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('e9ca8db8-c0ec-5fcb-91fb-f43364631c16','ffc2c9f9-78b8-59fc-9a56-332c0726f9a7',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a very high hill',null,null,'کوه، کوهستان؛ کوه (زیاد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['high These mountains are much higher than any in Europe.','rugged mountains (= rough and uneven ) the spectacular scenery of rugged mountains','a snow-capped mountain (= with snow on the top ) beautiful views of snow-capped mountains','a distant mountain (= far away ) The sun was setting over the distant mountains.','a great mountain (= a high, impressive mountain ) Here, great mountains are all around.','a sacred mountain (= considered holy ) Mount Fuji is a sacred mountain.','go/walk up a mountain ( also ascend a mountain formal ) Carrie and Albert went up the mountain, neither of them speaking as they climbed.','climb a mountain (= walk and/or climb to the top of a mountain ) Hillary had climbed all the big mountains in New Zealand.','go/walk down a mountain She lost her way as she went down the mountain.','cross the mountains We crossed the mountains between Spain and France.','mountains rise (= go high into the sky ) The mountains rise above the plains.','mountains soar/tower literary (= go very high into the sky ) The distant mountains soar abruptly towards the sky.','a mountain range/chain (= a number of mountains in a line ) The Alps are the largest mountain range in Europe.','a mountain top Until the end of June you may find snow on the mountain tops.','a mountain peak (= the top of a mountain ) Clouds hid the mountain peaks.','a mountain slope (= the sides of a mountain ) Snow lay on the steep mountain slopes.','a mountain pass (= a path or road between mountains ) Their journey took them through river valleys and over mountain passes.','a mountain stream The water was as clear and cold as a mountain stream.','mountain air a walk in the clear mountain air','mountain rescue (= people who help people who are in difficulty on a mountain ) Mountain rescue teams were called out to search for the missing climbers.','the top of a mountain ( also the summit of a mountain formal ) We climbed to the top of the mountain.','the foot of a mountain (= the bottom of a mountain ) We’ll take the car to the foot of the mountain and walk from there.','the side of a mountain The path wound up the side of the mountain.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the highest mountain in Austria","translation":"بلندترین کوه اتریش","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001759161.mp3"},{"sentence":"the Rocky Mountains","translation":"کوه های راکی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000212325.mp3"},{"sentence":"a steep mountain road","translation":"جاده کوهستانی شیب دار","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001566834.mp3"},{"sentence":"magnificent mountain ranges (= lines of mountains )","translation":"رشته کوه های باشکوه (= ردیف کوه ها)","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001759162.mp3"},{"sentence":"snow-capped mountain peaks (= tops of mountains )","translation":"قله های پوشیده از برف (= قله کوه ها)","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001665874.mp3"},{"sentence":"a mountain rescue team (= a group of experienced climbers who help people to safety from a mountain )","translation":"یک تیم نجات کوهستان (= گروهی از کوهنوردان با تجربه که به مردم کمک می کنند تا از کوه در امان بمانند)","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001817487.mp3"},{"sentence":"She was the first British woman to climb the mountain .","translation":"او اولین زن بریتانیایی بود که از کوه بالا رفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001817489.mp3"}]'::jsonb,7),
