('c000579c-9cc0-5a18-a00f-fb07ef5c49ea','d7483185-2733-5c19-8915-b115b6a8ba09',1,null,null,'spoken & written','someone that you do not know',null,null,'غریبه، ناآشنا؛ غریبه (فرد)؛ بیگانه (مجازی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a complete/perfect/total stranger (= used to emphasize that you do not know the person ) Really, I don''t know why I''m revealing all this to a complete stranger.','a virtual stranger (= someone you hardly know ) I hadn''t seen him for so long that he seemed like a virtual stranger.','a passing stranger (= one you pass in the street ) Do not give your camera to a passing stranger and ask him to take a picture of you.','a mysterious stranger She never knew who the mysterious stranger was who had helped her that night.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Children must not talk to strangers.","translation":"کودکان نباید با غریبه ها صحبت کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000619279.mp3"},{"sentence":"Julie finds it easy to speak to complete strangers.","translation":"برای جولی صحبت کردن با افراد کاملاً غریبه آسان است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001600025.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
