('86bf79e9-adca-57f1-b8e0-0847fb9edefe','70f80041-43d5-57c9-b345-b464ff2c5921',8,null,null,'spoken','used when saying in a joking way that you expected something to happen or be true',null,null,'وقتی به شوخی می گویید که انتظار دارید چیزی اتفاق بیفتد یا درست باشد استفاده می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['be a surprise His decision to marry was a complete surprise.','come as a surprise (= be surprising ) The announcement came as a surprise to most people.','get/have a surprise We got a surprise when we got home and found him waiting for us.','give somebody a surprise She wanted to give him a surprise.','have a surprise for somebody (= be planning to give someone a surprise ) I think Jenny might have a surprise for you.','spring a surprise (on somebody) (= give someone a surprise ) The chairman sprang a surprise this week by announcing his intention to quit.','a big/great surprise The results were a big surprise.','a complete/total surprise The news came as a complete surprise.','a nice/pleasant/lovely surprise It’s a lovely surprise to see you.','an unpleasant/nasty surprise We don’t want any unpleasant surprises.','come as no surprise (= not be surprising ) It came as no surprise when Lester got the job.','be in for a surprise (= be going to have a surprise ) Compare our prices. You’ll be in for a pleasant surprise.','there’s a surprise in store (for somebody) (= something unexpected is going to happen ) There were plenty more surprises in store for him.','a surprise visit Environmental health inspectors made a surprise visit to the restaurant.','a surprise party His friends had planned a surprise party for him.','a surprise announcement In a surprise announcement the company said they were withdrawing their planning application.','a surprise victory She came to power in 1977, after a surprise victory in the general election.','a surprise attack Instead they launched a successful surprise attack on the castle.','a surprise move (= an unexpected action ) In a surprise move, the government lifted the ban on arms exports to the country.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The American TV networks are, surprise, surprise, full of stories about the election.","translation":"شبکه های تلویزیونی آمریکا، غافلگیرکننده، غافلگیرکننده، پر از داستان درباره انتخابات هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000602321.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('982ca58a-0550-5645-8513-90cc30a47264','70f80041-43d5-57c9-b345-b464ff2c5921',9,'method','روش','spoken & written','the use of methods which are intended to cause surprise','[ uncountable ]',null,'استفاده از روش هایی که قصد دارند غافلگیر شوند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['be a surprise His decision to marry was a complete surprise.','come as a surprise (= be surprising ) The announcement came as a surprise to most people.','get/have a surprise We got a surprise when we got home and found him waiting for us.','give somebody a surprise She wanted to give him a surprise.','have a surprise for somebody (= be planning to give someone a surprise ) I think Jenny might have a surprise for you.','spring a surprise (on somebody) (= give someone a surprise ) The chairman sprang a surprise this week by announcing his intention to quit.','a big/great surprise The results were a big surprise.','a complete/total surprise The news came as a complete surprise.','a nice/pleasant/lovely surprise It’s a lovely surprise to see you.','an unpleasant/nasty surprise We don’t want any unpleasant surprises.','come as no surprise (= not be surprising ) It came as no surprise when Lester got the job.','be in for a surprise (= be going to have a surprise ) Compare our prices. You’ll be in for a pleasant surprise.','there’s a surprise in store (for somebody) (= something unexpected is going to happen ) There were plenty more surprises in store for him.','a surprise visit Environmental health inspectors made a surprise visit to the restaurant.','a surprise party His friends had planned a surprise party for him.','a surprise announcement In a surprise announcement the company said they were withdrawing their planning application.','a surprise victory She came to power in 1977, after a surprise victory in the general election.','a surprise attack Instead they launched a successful surprise attack on the castle.','a surprise move (= an unexpected action ) In a surprise move, the government lifted the ban on arms exports to the country.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"An element of surprise is important to any attack.","translation":"عنصر غافلگیری برای هر حمله ای مهم است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000602333.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('5671133f-e484-5dbf-a6d4-0da710ea0d7e','e6b99057-fe3d-549e-a653-d7d297da6284',1,null,null,'spoken','used when you are just about to show someone something that you know will surprise them',null,null,'وقتی می خواهید چیزی را به کسی نشان دهید که می دانید او را شگفت زده می کند استفاده می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('5a0b9d19-d64f-502a-8ca5-f6f9afc76789','5749d29a-55ca-533c-95e7-1d184a8547c6',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to make someone feel surprised',null,null,'برای اینکه کسی احساس تعجب کند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"His strange question surprised her.","translation":"سوال عجیب او او را شگفت زده کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000602343.mp3"},{"sentence":"It had surprised me to find how fussy he was about some things.","translation":"من را متعجب کرده بود که متوجه شدم او در مورد برخی چیزها چقدر دمدمی مزاج است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000602346.mp3"},{"sentence":"I didn’t know you two knew each other. Mind you, it doesn’t surprise me .","translation":"من نمیدونستم شما دوتا همدیگه رو میشناسید توجه داشته باشید، من را شگفت زده نمی کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000602349.mp3"},{"sentence":"What surprised me most was that she didn’t seem to care.","translation":"چیزی که بیش از همه مرا شگفت زده کرد این بود که به نظر نمی رسید او اهمیتی بدهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000602352.mp3"},{"sentence":"Looking back, does it surprise you that she left?","translation":"با نگاه کردن به گذشته، آیا شما را شگفت زده کرد که او رفت؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001616356.mp3"},{"sentence":"It wouldn’t surprise me if he married Jo.","translation":"اگر او با جو ازدواج کند، من را تعجب نمی کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001616357.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('c66cccdc-4d9c-5210-9c1c-20b76464f7ea','5749d29a-55ca-533c-95e7-1d184a8547c6',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to find, catch , or attack someone when they are not expecting it, especially when they are doing something they should not be doing',null,null,'پیدا کردن، گرفتن یا حمله کردن به کسی در زمانی که انتظارش را ندارد، به ویژه زمانی که دارد کاری را انجام می دهد که نباید انجام دهد.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"A security guard surprised the burglars in the storeroom.","translation":"یک نگهبان سارقان را در انبار غافلگیر کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000602365.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('53dba871-b41d-5a8a-99fc-a1169fa59b4d','6348b5c0-9a70-59fb-a140-50ca2d20998f',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to be all around someone or something on every side',null,null,'احاطه کردن، محاصره کردن (درب)؛ احاطه (حالت)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The field was surrounded by trees.","translation":"اطراف زمین را درختان احاطه کرده بودند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000602602.mp3"},{"sentence":"He glared at the people who surrounded the tent.","translation":"او به مردمی که اطراف چادر را احاطه کرده بودند خیره شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000602599.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('72bc2912-6963-5f39-ac90-f308128745c8','6348b5c0-9a70-59fb-a140-50ca2d20998f',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'be surrounded by somebody/something','احاطه کردن، محاصره کردن (درب)؛ احاطه (حالت)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('5f01e07a-0650-568f-ad1c-d2c3b2e2e6ae','6348b5c0-9a70-59fb-a140-50ca2d20998f',3,null,null,'spoken & written','if police or soldiers surround a place, they arrange themselves in positions all the way around it',null,null,'اگر پلیس یا سربازان مکانی را محاصره کنند، خود را در تمام نقاط اطراف آن قرار می دهند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Armed police surrounded a house in the High Street.","translation":"پلیس مسلح خانه ای را در خیابان High Street محاصره کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000602611.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('c5056773-08ed-5e48-87e4-2c5d819cf6eb','6348b5c0-9a70-59fb-a140-50ca2d20998f',4,null,null,'spoken & written','to be closely related to a situation or event',null,null,'ارتباط نزدیک با یک موقعیت یا رویداد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Some of the issues surrounding alcohol abuse are very complex.","translation":"برخی از مسائل مربوط به سوء مصرف الکل بسیار پیچیده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000602615.mp3"},{"sentence":"Silence and secrecy surround the murder.","translation":"سکوت و پنهان کاری اطراف قتل را احاطه کرده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001616426.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('8be61a33-f2be-56d6-99de-9bc1a8a72bc1','6348b5c0-9a70-59fb-a140-50ca2d20998f',5,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'surround yourself with somebody/something','احاطه کردن، محاصره کردن (درب)؛ احاطه (حالت)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('ff83f096-c01f-5d7a-8b2b-9394eb7e8297','7e5829c3-0613-5a2f-8949-76609fac871f',1,null,null,'spoken & written','an area around the edge of something, especially one that is decorated or made of a different material',null,null,'ناحیه ای در اطراف لبه چیزی، به ویژه جایی که تزئین شده یا از مواد دیگری ساخته شده است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a solid mahogany fire surround","translation":"آتش ماهون جامد احاطه شده است","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001616427.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('4231aac6-a351-5529-9ce0-e2bc3ff08635','40bcc788-4242-5880-bbd4-bd42637b4875',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the state of continuing to live or exist','[ uncountable ]',null,'بقا، بقای (حیات)؛ بقای (شرکت)؛ زنده‌ماندن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['long-term survival The long-term survival of polar bears is at risk.','continued survival The continued survival of this species of dolphin seems unlikely.','economic survival Both countries depend on wildlife-based tourism for their economic survival.','political survival The prime minister is fighting for his political survival.','the survival rate The survival rate of animals returned to the wild remains an unanswered question.','somebody’s survival instinct (= a natural ability to know how to survive ) My survival instinct told me to get up and run.','survival skills They learned survival skills from the local Indian tribe.','a survival strategy The best survival strategy is to avoid putting yourself in unnecessary danger.','fight/struggle for survival Many construction companies are fighting for survival.','ensure the survival of something/somebody Controlling land development would ensure the survival of many types of wildlife.','owe your survival to somebody/something The frogs owe their survival to a conservation program.','somebody’s chance(s) of survival He knew that his chances of survival were small.','somebody’s fight/struggle/battle for survival Their lives had been one long struggle for survival.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Illegal hunting is threatening the survival of the species.","translation":"شکار غیرقانونی بقای این گونه را تهدید می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001616258.mp3"},{"sentence":"The doctors gave him a one in ten chance of survival .","translation":"پزشکان به او شانس زنده ماندن یک در ده دادند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001616259.mp3"},{"sentence":"A lot of small companies are having to fight for survival (= work hard in order to continue to exist ) .","translation":"بسیاری از شرکت های کوچک مجبورند برای بقا بجنگند (= سخت کار کنند تا به حیات خود ادامه دهند).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000602773.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('6675d1a0-d7c6-500b-bc4a-296631fc5af8','40bcc788-4242-5880-bbd4-bd42637b4875',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'survival of the fittest','بقا، بقای (حیات)؛ بقای (شرکت)؛ زنده‌ماندن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['long-term survival The long-term survival of polar bears is at risk.','continued survival The continued survival of this species of dolphin seems unlikely.','economic survival Both countries depend on wildlife-based tourism for their economic survival.','political survival The prime minister is fighting for his political survival.','the survival rate The survival rate of animals returned to the wild remains an unanswered question.','somebody’s survival instinct (= a natural ability to know how to survive ) My survival instinct told me to get up and run.','survival skills They learned survival skills from the local Indian tribe.','a survival strategy The best survival strategy is to avoid putting yourself in unnecessary danger.','fight/struggle for survival Many construction companies are fighting for survival.','ensure the survival of something/somebody Controlling land development would ensure the survival of many types of wildlife.','owe your survival to somebody/something The frogs owe their survival to a conservation program.','somebody’s chance(s) of survival He knew that his chances of survival were small.','somebody’s fight/struggle/battle for survival Their lives had been one long struggle for survival.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('5e827af0-65cd-5948-86e8-9825d6116df8','40bcc788-4242-5880-bbd4-bd42637b4875',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'a survival from something','بقا، بقای (حیات)؛ بقای (شرکت)؛ زنده‌ماندن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['long-term survival The long-term survival of polar bears is at risk.','continued survival The continued survival of this species of dolphin seems unlikely.','economic survival Both countries depend on wildlife-based tourism for their economic survival.','political survival The prime minister is fighting for his political survival.','the survival rate The survival rate of animals returned to the wild remains an unanswered question.','somebody’s survival instinct (= a natural ability to know how to survive ) My survival instinct told me to get up and run.','survival skills They learned survival skills from the local Indian tribe.','a survival strategy The best survival strategy is to avoid putting yourself in unnecessary danger.','fight/struggle for survival Many construction companies are fighting for survival.','ensure the survival of something/somebody Controlling land development would ensure the survival of many types of wildlife.','owe your survival to somebody/something The frogs owe their survival to a conservation program.','somebody’s chance(s) of survival He knew that his chances of survival were small.','somebody’s fight/struggle/battle for survival Their lives had been one long struggle for survival.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('85b1b61b-58af-5e70-a82b-8191816ff018','873913be-f386-57af-8dcf-e9ac12161ed2',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the sport of moving yourself through water using your arms and legs',null,null,'شنا، شنایی (ورزش)؛ شنا (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Swimming is great exercise.","translation":"شنا ورزش عالی است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000605976.mp3"},{"sentence":"a swimming club","translation":"یک باشگاه شنا","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000605977.mp3"},{"sentence":"We went swimming on Saturday.","translation":"شنبه رفتیم شنا.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001984925.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('2763a6ff-5e65-5769-a9a6-a5a7f0364ec8','95bfd227-263c-5655-bb89-5d6ff69b114a',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the feeling of being sorry for someone who is in a bad situation','[ plural, uncountable ]',null,'دلسوزی، ترحم؛ همدلی (فرد)؛ همدردی (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have/feel sympathy for somebody It’s hard not to feel sympathy for the losing team.','express/offer (your) sympathy Everyone there expressed their sympathy.','get sympathy from somebody I thought at least I’d get some sympathy from you.','deserve sympathy He doesn''t deserve any sympathy - it''s his own fault.','play on somebody’s sympathy (= make someone feel sorry for you in order to get an advantage for yourself ) If that doesn’t work, she knows how to play on his sympathy.','expect sympathy I know I can’t expect any sympathy from her!','deep/deepest sympathy (= used when someone is upset after a death ) We''d like to offer our deepest sympathy to Hilda and her family.','great sympathy I have great sympathy for the people affected by the housing crisis.','a message/letter of sympathy We are grateful for all the messages of sympathy we have received.','an expression of sympathy I murmured an expression of sympathy.','have every sympathy for somebody (= feel very sorry for someone - often used when you have had a similar experience yourself ) I have every sympathy for people who find it hard to give up smoking.','you have my sympathy (= used when saying that you feel sorry for someone ) It must be difficult – you have my sympathy.','extend your sympathy to somebody formal (= express sympathy ) I’d like to extend my deepest sympathy to the victim’s family.','my/our sympathy goes out to somebody formal (= used to formally express sympathy ) Our sympathy goes out to Peggy in her great loss.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"I have a lot of sympathy for her; she had to bring up the children on her own.","translation":"من خیلی برای او همدردی دارم. او مجبور بود بچه ها را خودش بزرگ کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000607619.mp3"},{"sentence":"I have absolutely no sympathy for students who get caught cheating in exams.","translation":"من مطلقاً با دانش آموزانی که در امتحانات در حال تقلب می شوند، همدردی نمی کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001621954.mp3"},{"sentence":"Our sympathies are with the families of the victims.","translation":"همدردی ما با خانواده های قربانیان است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001621968.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('856e825b-cebf-5b58-b4b3-6fee057d13a3','95bfd227-263c-5655-bb89-5d6ff69b114a',2,null,null,'spoken & written','belief in or support for a plan, idea, or action , especially a political one','[ plural, uncountable ]',null,'اعتقاد یا حمایت از یک طرح، ایده یا اقدام، به ویژه یک طرح سیاسی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have/feel sympathy for somebody It’s hard not to feel sympathy for the losing team.','express/offer (your) sympathy Everyone there expressed their sympathy.','get sympathy from somebody I thought at least I’d get some sympathy from you.','deserve sympathy He doesn''t deserve any sympathy - it''s his own fault.','play on somebody’s sympathy (= make someone feel sorry for you in order to get an advantage for yourself ) If that doesn’t work, she knows how to play on his sympathy.','expect sympathy I know I can’t expect any sympathy from her!','deep/deepest sympathy (= used when someone is upset after a death ) We''d like to offer our deepest sympathy to Hilda and her family.','great sympathy I have great sympathy for the people affected by the housing crisis.','a message/letter of sympathy We are grateful for all the messages of sympathy we have received.','an expression of sympathy I murmured an expression of sympathy.','have every sympathy for somebody (= feel very sorry for someone - often used when you have had a similar experience yourself ) I have every sympathy for people who find it hard to give up smoking.','you have my sympathy (= used when saying that you feel sorry for someone ) It must be difficult – you have my sympathy.','extend your sympathy to somebody formal (= express sympathy ) I’d like to extend my deepest sympathy to the victim’s family.','my/our sympathy goes out to somebody formal (= used to formally express sympathy ) Our sympathy goes out to Peggy in her great loss.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Willard is in sympathy with many Green Party issues.","translation":"ویلارد با بسیاری از مسائل حزب سبز همدردی می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001621976.mp3"},{"sentence":"Her sympathies lie firmly with the Conservative Party.","translation":"همدردی او با حزب محافظه کار است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001621977.mp3"},{"sentence":"Matheson is known for his pro-socialist sympathies.","translation":"متسون به خاطر همدردی‌های طرفدار سوسیالیست‌اش معروف است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001621985.mp3"},{"sentence":"Sullivan expressed sympathy for the striking federal workers.","translation":"سالیوان با کارگران فدرال اعتصابی ابراز همدردی کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001621988.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('f9f8a56b-7b1b-55c2-bd05-55e313608293','95bfd227-263c-5655-bb89-5d6ff69b114a',3,null,null,'spoken & written','a feeling that you understand someone because you are similar to them','[ uncountable ]',null,'احساس اینکه شما کسی را درک می کنید زیرا شبیه او هستید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have/feel sympathy for somebody It’s hard not to feel sympathy for the losing team.','express/offer (your) sympathy Everyone there expressed their sympathy.','get sympathy from somebody I thought at least I’d get some sympathy from you.','deserve sympathy He doesn''t deserve any sympathy - it''s his own fault.','play on somebody’s sympathy (= make someone feel sorry for you in order to get an advantage for yourself ) If that doesn’t work, she knows how to play on his sympathy.','expect sympathy I know I can’t expect any sympathy from her!','deep/deepest sympathy (= used when someone is upset after a death ) We''d like to offer our deepest sympathy to Hilda and her family.','great sympathy I have great sympathy for the people affected by the housing crisis.','a message/letter of sympathy We are grateful for all the messages of sympathy we have received.','an expression of sympathy I murmured an expression of sympathy.','have every sympathy for somebody (= feel very sorry for someone - often used when you have had a similar experience yourself ) I have every sympathy for people who find it hard to give up smoking.','you have my sympathy (= used when saying that you feel sorry for someone ) It must be difficult – you have my sympathy.','extend your sympathy to somebody formal (= express sympathy ) I’d like to extend my deepest sympathy to the victim’s family.','my/our sympathy goes out to somebody formal (= used to formally express sympathy ) Our sympathy goes out to Peggy in her great loss.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"There was no personal sympathy between them.","translation":"هیچ همدردی شخصی بین آنها وجود نداشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001621989.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('8bc07c90-3e5f-511a-8e3a-49f57c165b5b','77f0b820-6782-58aa-b3bd-b7cc06bc6333',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the work or profession of a teacher',null,null,'تدریس، آموزش؛ تعلیم (فرد)؛ تدریس (پرستار)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['language/English/science etc teaching She has considerable experience in language teaching.','the teaching profession (= teachers, or the career of teaching ) Many of our undergraduates subsequently enter the teaching profession.','the teaching staff (= the teachers at a school, college etc ) She attended a girls'' school where all the teaching staff were women.','teaching methods Our teaching methods are quite traditional.','teaching materials This will help teachers to prepare their own teaching materials.','a teaching aid (= a piece of equipment that a teacher uses in the classroom ) The school is equipped with modern teaching aids, including interactive whiteboards.','teaching practice British English , student teaching American English (= a period of teaching done by someone who is training to be a teacher ) There were 90 hours of teaching practice, of which 20 were supervised.','a teaching job/post I was soon to take up my first teaching post.','a teaching career She began her teaching career at a school in inner London.','a teaching establishment (= a school, college, or university ) Every higher education teaching establishment is subject to rigorous scrutiny.','go into teaching (= become a teacher ) Some very talented and dedicated people go into teaching.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Mrs Ward had many years of experience in teaching.","translation":"خانم وارد سالها تجربه تدریس داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa020283.mp3"},{"sentence":"She’s thinking of going into teaching (= becoming a teacher ) .","translation":"او در فکر رفتن به تدریس (= معلم شدن) است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001587491.mp3"},{"sentence":"extra funding for English teaching in schools","translation":"بودجه اضافی برای آموزش زبان انگلیسی در مدارس","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001580.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('22196304-511d-50ff-b252-4221d2875422','77f0b820-6782-58aa-b3bd-b7cc06bc6333',2,null,null,'spoken & written','the moral , religious , or political ideas of a particular person or group which are taught to other people','[ plural ]',null,'عقاید اخلاقی، مذهبی یا سیاسی یک فرد یا گروه خاص که به افراد دیگر آموزش داده می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['language/English/science etc teaching She has considerable experience in language teaching.','the teaching profession (= teachers, or the career of teaching ) Many of our undergraduates subsequently enter the teaching profession.','the teaching staff (= the teachers at a school, college etc ) She attended a girls'' school where all the teaching staff were women.','teaching methods Our teaching methods are quite traditional.','teaching materials This will help teachers to prepare their own teaching materials.','a teaching aid (= a piece of equipment that a teacher uses in the classroom ) The school is equipped with modern teaching aids, including interactive whiteboards.','teaching practice British English , student teaching American English (= a period of teaching done by someone who is training to be a teacher ) There were 90 hours of teaching practice, of which 20 were supervised.','a teaching job/post I was soon to take up my first teaching post.','a teaching career She began her teaching career at a school in inner London.','a teaching establishment (= a school, college, or university ) Every higher education teaching establishment is subject to rigorous scrutiny.','go into teaching (= become a teacher ) Some very talented and dedicated people go into teaching.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the teachings of Gandhi","translation":"آموزه های گاندی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000584079.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('d416731d-e9c3-55a5-abf5-5afd3ae81546','4bffc8d3-32fb-5dba-ab15-695a3613eee9',1,null,null,'spoken & written','if someone or something has a tendency to do or become a particular thing, they are likely to do or become it',null,null,'گرایش، میل (ذهنی)؛ گرایش (فرد)؛ گرایش (رشد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a natural tendency (= one you are born with ) His recent experiences had reinforced a strong natural tendency towards caution.','an inherent/innate tendency (= one that you are born with, which will not change ) When attacked, some people have an inherent tendency to fight back.','a strong tendency There is a strong tendency to give dying patients far more drugs than are necessary.','a marked tendency (= noticeable ) There is a marked tendency for Hollywood marriages to end in divorce.','aggressive/violent tendencies Some breeds of dog have aggressive tendencies.','suicidal tendencies They failed to inform the prison authorities of the man''s suicidal tendencies.','criminal tendencies How should we deal with young people who have criminal tendencies?','artistic tendencies As he grew up, he displayed artistic tendencies.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Greg’s tendency to be critical made him unpopular with his co-workers.","translation":"تمایل گرگ به انتقاد پذیری باعث شد که او در بین همکارانش محبوبیت نداشته باشد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001616652.mp3"},{"sentence":"The drug is effective but has a tendency to cause headaches.","translation":"این دارو موثر است اما تمایل به ایجاد سردرد دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001616655.mp3"},{"sentence":"Some people may inherit a tendency to alcoholism.","translation":"برخی از افراد ممکن است تمایل به اعتیاد به الکل را به ارث ببرند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000590279.mp3"},{"sentence":"Researchers believe that the tendency for diabetes is present at birth.","translation":"محققان معتقدند که تمایل به دیابت از بدو تولد وجود دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001616658.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('397a824e-fac8-5fb1-a32e-90070bef3635','4bffc8d3-32fb-5dba-ab15-695a3613eee9',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a general change or development in a particular direction',null,null,'یک تغییر یا توسعه کلی در یک جهت خاص','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"There is an increasing tendency for women to have children later in life.","translation":"تمایل زنان به بچه دار شدن در مراحل بعدی زندگی رو به افزایش است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001616661.mp3"},{"sentence":"a general tendency towards conservation and recycling","translation":"گرایش کلی به حفاظت و بازیافت","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000590297.mp3"},{"sentence":"a tendency among Americans to get married at a later age","translation":"تمایل آمریکایی ها به ازدواج در سنین بالاتر","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001616664.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('7000bfea-9a67-58e2-af05-09c4cc98c1ef','4bffc8d3-32fb-5dba-ab15-695a3613eee9',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'aggressive/suicidal/criminal/artistic etc tendencies','گرایش، میل (ذهنی)؛ گرایش (فرد)؛ گرایش (رشد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a natural tendency (= one you are born with ) His recent experiences had reinforced a strong natural tendency towards caution.','an inherent/innate tendency (= one that you are born with, which will not change ) When attacked, some people have an inherent tendency to fight back.','a strong tendency There is a strong tendency to give dying patients far more drugs than are necessary.','a marked tendency (= noticeable ) There is a marked tendency for Hollywood marriages to end in divorce.','aggressive/violent tendencies Some breeds of dog have aggressive tendencies.','suicidal tendencies They failed to inform the prison authorities of the man''s suicidal tendencies.','criminal tendencies How should we deal with young people who have criminal tendencies?','artistic tendencies As he grew up, he displayed artistic tendencies.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('c473db30-107e-526c-bfe9-5213c29cb900','4bffc8d3-32fb-5dba-ab15-695a3613eee9',4,null,null,'spoken & written','a group within a larger political group that supports ideas that are usually more extreme than those of the main group',null,null,'گروهی در درون یک گروه سیاسی بزرگتر که از ایده هایی حمایت می کند که معمولاً افراطی تر از ایده های گروه اصلی است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"the growing fascist tendency","translation":"گرایش فاشیستی رو به رشد","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000590304.mp3"},{"sentence":"The extremist tendency is becoming more powerful.","translation":"گرایش افراطی در حال قدرتمندتر شدن است.","audio_url":null},{"sentence":"The extremist tendency are becoming more powerful.","translation":"گرایش افراطی در حال قدرتمندتر شدن است.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,3),
('a50acef0-26ae-577b-b853-85924e22451a','cd1b3554-4f79-5dd8-a5eb-2ff9717cad4b',1,null,null,'spoken & written','extremely severe in a way that causes harm or damage',null,null,'هولناک، فجیع؛ شدید (درد)؛ بد (حالت)',array['horrible','awful']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Their son had been injured in a terrible accident.","translation":"پسرشان در یک تصادف وحشتناک مجروح شده بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000591537.mp3"},{"sentence":"We’re worried that something terrible might have happened to Greg.","translation":"ما نگران هستیم که ممکن است اتفاق وحشتناکی برای گرگ رخ داده باشد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001616859.mp3"},{"sentence":"a terrible storm","translation":"یک طوفان وحشتناک","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001616860.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('bc719b3f-9967-5bef-aa79-019315492371','cd1b3554-4f79-5dd8-a5eb-2ff9717cad4b',2,null,null,'spoken & written','very bad',null,null,'خیلی بد',array['awful']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The hotel was absolutely terrible.","translation":"هتل کاملا وحشتناک بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000591552.mp3"},{"sentence":"I’d better write this down; I have a terrible memory.","translation":"بهتر است این را بنویسم؛ حافظه وحشتناکی دارم","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000591553.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('ee303ba4-9e3c-5d58-b88b-d35fb60d9161','cd1b3554-4f79-5dd8-a5eb-2ff9717cad4b',3,null,null,'spoken & written','making you feel afraid or shocked',null,null,'باعث می شود احساس ترس یا شوکه کنید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"There was a terrible noise and the roof caved in.","translation":"صدای وحشتناکی شنیده شد و سقف فرو رفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000591542.mp3"},{"sentence":"She wept when she heard the terrible news.","translation":"با شنیدن این خبر وحشتناک گریه کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001616862.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('7975ee68-55dc-5302-a76f-96bf19d618c9','cd1b3554-4f79-5dd8-a5eb-2ff9717cad4b',4,null,null,'spoken & written','to a very great degree',null,null,'به درجه بسیار عالی',array['grave']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"You’re making a terrible mistake.","translation":"شما یک اشتباه وحشتناک مرتکب می شوید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001616866.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('27c5f9b6-d1e2-5892-a03c-1c0ce7288ca6','6825b5b4-bbbb-5fcc-b50a-338c0df3a63c',1,null,null,'spoken & written','very','[ +adj/adverb ]',null,'فجیعاً، به‌شدت؛ خیلی (تأکید)',array['extremely']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I’m terribly sorry to have kept you waiting.","translation":"خیلی متاسفم که منتظرت گذاشتم","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000591569.mp3"},{"sentence":"The coach was not terribly worried about his team’s poor performance.","translation":"مربی خیلی نگران عملکرد ضعیف تیمش نبود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001616867.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('a57fbbaa-7e66-5d1e-a01c-801c2b5b6ee6','6825b5b4-bbbb-5fcc-b50a-338c0df3a63c',2,null,null,'spoken & written','very badly',null,null,'خیلی بد',array['severely']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The little boy missed his mother terribly.","translation":"پسر کوچولو به شدت دلتنگ مادرش شده بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000591574.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('2a3d89cd-43da-56d3-b0fe-fa46704840cf','3f232f06-1f53-554c-b7d8-cf60e6614662',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to say that you will cause someone harm or trouble if they do not do what you want','[ transitive ]',null,'تهدید کردن؛ ترسانیدن (فرد)؛ پیش‌آگهی (طوفان)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Postal workers are threatening a strike if they don’t receive a pay increase.","translation":"کارکنان پست در صورت عدم افزایش حقوق تهدید به اعتصاب می کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001645070.mp3"},{"sentence":"He threatened to take them to court.","translation":"او تهدید کرد که آنها را به دادگاه خواهد برد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001645073.mp3"},{"sentence":"Doctors are sometimes threatened with violence if they don’t do what patients want.","translation":"اگر پزشکان خواسته‌های بیماران را انجام ندهند، گاهی به خشونت تهدید می‌شوند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000567027.mp3"},{"sentence":"Then he became angry and threatened that he would go to the police.","translation":"سپس عصبانی شد و تهدید کرد که به پلیس خواهد رفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001645078.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('4f5a2a43-950d-5f1d-a473-64529c185420','3f232f06-1f53-554c-b7d8-cf60e6614662',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to be likely to harm or destroy something','[ transitive ]',null,'احتمال آسیب رساندن یا تخریب چیزی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Poaching threatens the survival of the rhino.","translation":"شکار غیرقانونی بقای کرگدن را تهدید می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000567041.mp3"},{"sentence":"The incident threatens to ruin his chances in the election.","translation":"این حادثه شانس او ​​را در انتخابات از بین می برد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000567051.mp3"},{"sentence":"Large areas of the jungle are now threatened with destruction.","translation":"اکنون مناطق وسیعی از جنگل در معرض نابودی قرار دارند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001645083.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('2886e79e-0d87-5f0e-96f5-0015f6909bd4','3f232f06-1f53-554c-b7d8-cf60e6614662',3,null,null,'spoken & written','to be likely to happen or be in a bad situation','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'احتمال وقوع یا قرار گرفتن در موقعیت بدی وجود دارد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Britain’s fishing industry remains threatened.","translation":"صنعت ماهیگیری بریتانیا همچنان در معرض تهدید است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001645087.mp3"},{"sentence":"Dark clouds threatened rain.","translation":"ابرهای تیره باران را تهدید می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001645088.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('68cd3512-357d-522e-a7ca-78531c15558b','9a253741-999f-54ff-bd5b-71d4421674d7',1,'with each other','با یکدیگر','spoken & written','if two or more people do something together, they do it with each other',null,null,'با هم، همدیگر؛ یکجا؛ هم‌زمان (تلفن)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"We’ve very much enjoyed working together .","translation":"ما از کار با هم بسیار لذت بردیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001603257.mp3"},{"sentence":"They’ve decided to spend more time together.","translation":"آنها تصمیم گرفته اند زمان بیشتری را با هم بگذرانند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000576431.mp3"},{"sentence":"He and my father were at school together.","translation":"او و پدرم با هم در مدرسه بودند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000576429.mp3"},{"sentence":"Together they went back inside the villa.","translation":"با هم به داخل ویلا برگشتند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001603258.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('cbe0df7f-a93d-5315-a15f-89a8de1617fe','9a253741-999f-54ff-bd5b-71d4421674d7',2,'make one thing','یک چیز بساز','spoken & written','if you put two or more things together, you join them so that they touch or form one whole thing or group',null,null,'اگر دو یا چند چیز را کنار هم قرار دهید، به آنها می پیوندید تا یک چیز یا گروه کامل را لمس کنند یا تشکیل دهند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"He’d tried to glue the broken pieces together.","translation":"او سعی کرده بود قطعات شکسته را به هم بچسباند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000576406.mp3"},{"sentence":"Mix the butter and sugar together.","translation":"کره و شکر را با هم مخلوط کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000576404.mp3"},{"sentence":"She clasped her hands together.","translation":"دستانش را به هم قلاب کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001603259.mp3"},{"sentence":"He took the engine apart and then put it back together again.","translation":"موتور را از هم جدا کرد و دوباره سر هم کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001603260.mp3"},{"sentence":"The model was held together with string.","translation":"این مدل با نخ در کنار هم نگه داشته شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000576407.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('da954fbd-e360-5da5-8919-714db172311b','9a253741-999f-54ff-bd5b-71d4421674d7',3,'be a couple','زن و شوهر باشند','spoken & written','if two people are together, they are married , or are having a romantic or sexual relationship',null,null,'اگر دو نفر با هم باشند، ازدواج کرده اند یا رابطه عاشقانه یا جنسی دارند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Mark and I have been together eight years now.","translation":"من و مارک الان هشت سال با هم هستیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001603271.mp3"},{"sentence":"Are those two together?","translation":"آیا آن دو با هم هستند؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001603272.mp3"},{"sentence":"A lot of people live together before getting married.","translation":"بسیاری از افراد قبل از ازدواج با هم زندگی می کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001603277.mp3"},{"sentence":"Sometimes I don’t know what keeps us together .","translation":"گاهی اوقات نمی دانم چه چیزی ما را با هم نگه می دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001603281.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('de9e8085-0cd2-5ed1-bab6-fc1cb6ff7b83','9a253741-999f-54ff-bd5b-71d4421674d7',4,'in one place','در یک مکان','spoken & written','if you keep, collect etc things together, you keep or collect them all in one place',null,null,'اگر چیزهای دیگری را با هم نگه دارید، جمع آوری کنید، همه آنها را در یک مکان نگه می دارید یا جمع می کنید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"She keeps all the important documents together in one file.","translation":"او تمام اسناد مهم را با هم در یک پرونده نگه می دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001603287.mp3"},{"sentence":"Embarrassed, she gathered her things together and left.","translation":"خجالت زده وسایلش را جمع کرد و رفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001603288.mp3"},{"sentence":"Goods of a similar kind should be stored together.","translation":"کالاهای مشابه باید در کنار هم نگهداری شوند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001603289.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('fc220ddb-0108-59ef-bb4a-e60ad9ce0767','9a253741-999f-54ff-bd5b-71d4421674d7',5,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'close/packed/crowded etc together','با هم، همدیگر؛ یکجا؛ هم‌زمان (تلفن)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('ec5cdea4-4646-55a6-8ec8-5d428b6717b6','9a253741-999f-54ff-bd5b-71d4421674d7',6,'against each other','در برابر یکدیگر','spoken & written','if you rub or hit things together, you rub or hit them against each other',null,null,'اگر چیزها را به هم مالش دهید یا به هم بزنید، آنها را به هم می مالید یا می زنید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Max was rubbing his hands together with glee.","translation":"مکس با خوشحالی دست هایش را به هم می مالید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000576423.mp3"},{"sentence":"Knock the brushes together to clean them.","translation":"برس ها را به هم بزنید تا تمیز شوند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000576424.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('b5d67138-32f9-5181-9298-54cf5baad397','9a253741-999f-54ff-bd5b-71d4421674d7',7,'in agreement','در توافق','spoken & written','if people are together, come together etc, they are or become united , especially in order to try and achieve something',null,null,'اگر مردم با هم باشند، گرد هم آیند و غیره، متحد می شوند یا متحد می شوند، به ویژه برای تلاش و رسیدن به چیزی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Together we can win.","translation":"با هم می توانیم پیروز شویم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000576442.mp3"},{"sentence":"The Conference called on all good men to come together to resist terrorism.","translation":"کنفرانس از همه مردان خوب خواست تا برای مقاومت در برابر تروریسم گرد هم آیند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001603291.mp3"},{"sentence":"He said that the main purpose of the Baha''i faith was to bring people together .","translation":"وی هدف اصلی بهائیت را گرد هم آوردن مردم دانست.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000576444.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('1b0cc193-bf84-52f4-a911-903b98532f74','9a253741-999f-54ff-bd5b-71d4421674d7',8,'at the same time','در همان زمان','spoken & written','at the same time',null,null,'در همان زمان','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Both letters should have arrived. I mailed them together.","translation":"هر دو نامه باید می رسید. من آنها را با هم پست کردم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001603304.mp3"},{"sentence":"‘Oh!’ they said together.","translation":"با هم گفتند: \"اوه!\"","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001603305.mp3"},{"sentence":"Right men. All together now ... push!","translation":"مردان حق همه با هم اکنون ... فشار دهید!","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000576437.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('675078e0-20e5-5405-ae21-0e9862a9cfb0','9a253741-999f-54ff-bd5b-71d4421674d7',9,'combine amounts','مقادیر را ترکیب کنید','spoken & written','when two amounts or quantities are added together, they are combined',null,null,'وقتی دو مقدار یا مقدار با هم جمع می شوند، با هم ترکیب می شوند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Add these numbers together and then divide the total by 7.","translation":"این اعداد را با هم جمع کرده و مجموع را بر 7 تقسیم کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001603311.mp3"},{"sentence":"Together they won only 21% of the votes.","translation":"آنها با هم تنها 21 درصد آرا را به دست آوردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001603312.mp3"},{"sentence":"The table and chairs are together worth about £200.","translation":"میز و صندلی با هم حدود 200 پوند ارزش دارند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001603313.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
